eir hands after diaper changes, but the older infants were not having their hands washed in the hand washing sink after diapering or before eating lunch.","topic":"sanitation","source_record_id":"1026468988","violation_type_title":"Children Handwashing After Toileting or Diapering (26 TAC §746.3417(3))","topic_label":"Sanitation & hygiene"}]},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1375111-i20221216","date":"2022-12-16","inspection_type":"Inspection","result":"Deficiencies cited","passed":false,"violation_count":5,"open_count":0,"evidence_class":"VERIFIED","provenance":{"source_id":"tx_hhsc_activities","source_record_id":"905848077","url":"https://data.texas.gov/resource/m5q4-3y3d.json?activity_id=905848077","retrieved_at":"2026-11-05T21:27:29.718Z","effective_date":"2022-12-16","evidence_class":"VERIFIED"},"occurrences":[{"id":"tx-hhsc-1375111-i20221216-v1","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-3505-e","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1375111-i20221216","date":"2022-12-16","original_code":"746.3505(e)","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2022-12-20","finding":"Diapering Procedures - Sanitizing Diaper Changing Area: Multiple diaper changes were observed and the sanitizing surface was not cleaned after the diaper changes surface. The surface is a hard surface that did not have wax paper utilized.","topic":"sanitation","source_record_id":"1026389438","violation_type_title":"Diapering Procedures - Sanitizing Diaper Changing Area (26 TAC §746.3505(e))","topic_label":"Sanitation & hygiene"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1375111-i20221216-v2","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-3417-3","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1375111-i20221216","date":"2022-12-16","original_code":"746.3417(3)","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2022-12-20","finding":"Children Handwashing After Toileting or Diapering: Diaper changes were conducted in the older infant classroom. Various diaper changes were observed and the infants and the staff did not wash their hands after any of the diaper changes. Additionally, the infants hands were not washed prior to eating. Staff were observed cleaning children's noses and also did not wash their hands.","topic":"sanitation","source_record_id":"1026509660","violation_type_title":"Children Handwashing After Toileting or Diapering (26 TAC §746.3417(3))","topic_label":"Sanitation & hygiene"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1375111-i20221216-v3","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-3425-3","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1375111-i20221216","date":"2022-12-16","original_code":"746.3425(3)","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2022-12-20","finding":"Disposing of Gloves after One Use: Gloves were not able to be disposed of immediately use it's use and a child was able to pick it up and place it in their mouth.","topic":"other","source_record_id":"1026509661","violation_type_title":"Disposing of Gloves after One Use (26 TAC §746.3425(3))","topic_label":"Other"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1375111-i20221216-v4","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-3505-f","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1375111-i20221216","date":"2022-12-16","original_code":"746.3505(f)","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2022-12-20","finding":"Diapering Procedures-Soiled Diapers Kept in a Sanitary Manner: Diapers that were disposed of in a shared bathroom for older children, were in a trash receptacle that does not have a lid and is accessible to children in care.","topic":"safety","source_record_id":"1026349207","violation_type_title":"Diapering Procedures-Soiled Diapers Kept in a Sanitary Manner (26 TAC §746.3505(f))","topic_label":"Safety hazards"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1375111-i20221216-v5","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-2501-4","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1375111-i20221216","date":"2022-12-16","original_code":"746.2501(4)","severity":"medium_high","severity_